# wave_swap_udp — the one human, over the wire.
#
# Ready only. start_game is refused in --server mode, so what starts the round
# here is the lobby's own all-ready check: this ready plus the held seats,
# which are seated ready as every bot seat is. Everything after that is the
# scenario beside the map, which fields a wave into the seats its lobby is
# holding, hands them back between waves, and ends the round itself.
#
# The slot is 6, not 0. The scenario's lobby template seats its six raiders
# before anybody joins and the free-slot rule hands out the first slot nobody
# is in, so the seats hold 0-5 and this client lands in 6. set_ready in
# --server mode refuses any slot but the client's own and exits 2, so a
# template that seated a different number would fail here rather than quietly
# readying the wrong seat.
#
# The tick is the client's own pump counter, about a millisecond an iteration
# while the server tick is still 0, so this is roughly three seconds in — well
# past the join and the map download.
#
# No exit op: the run ends on the server's shutdown, not on anything here.
{"tick": 3000, "op": "set_ready", "slot": 6, "ready": true}
